      "claim": "The medieval English economic system was based on feudalism and manorialism.",
      "evidence": "Historical consensus defines the social and economic structure of medieval England as feudal, where lords held land and peasants (serfs or villeins) worked it in exchange for protection and the right to farm small plots.",
