      "claim": "Peasants were legally bound to the land and owed specific labor services (corvée) to the lord.",
      "evidence": "Serfdom and villeinage required peasants to work the lord's demesne for a set number of days per week, a non-negotiable obligation rather than a market transaction.",
      "weight": 0.9,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
